+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,136 @@
+# Skew-brace class identification from holomorph generators
+
+**Status:** locally verified candidate; **not yet shippable** because the required
+OpenRouter oracle runs were blocked by HTTP 403 quota errors.  G1--G8 pass.  G9's
+size/effort caps pass, but its oracle-polarity test has no scored attempts.
+
+| Profile field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B** — an efficient algorithm exists and is disclosed |
+| Native domain / regime | algebra / finite discrete |
+| Computational core | other (finite group and holomorph computation) |
+| Certificate | integer tuple of skew-brace class parameters |
+| Native objects | `Z_p semidirect Z_q`, its automorphisms, regular holomorph subgroups |
+| Intuition | invariant: the second-coordinate projection survives additive-automorphism conjugation |
+| Domain essentiality | native; no reduction |
+
+## The problem
+
+The source is Acri and Bonatto, [*Skew braces of size pq*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.03228).
+An instance displays several regular subgroups of the holomorph of the paper's
+nonabelian group `M = Z_p semidirect Z_q`.  Each subgroup is given by shuffled,
+conjugated generators plus redundant generators.  The solver must identify the
+paper's isomorphism-class parameter `mu` for the skew brace induced by each
+subgroup.  Verification extracts the invariant `d` from the displayed generators
+and checks `d*(mu-1) == 1 (mod q)`, using exact integer arithmetic only.
+
+Section 1 and Theorem 1.3 fix the regular-subgroup-to-brace definition.  Section 2
+defines `M` and its automorphisms.  Lemma 3.10, Proposition 3.11, and Theorem 3.12
+give the precise nonabelian, trivial-kernel regime used here.  The easy regimes are
+excluded: Proposition 3.1 leaves only the trivial brace when `p` is not `1 mod q`,
+and Theorem 3.4 leaves only one nontrivial cyclic-type brace.
+
+## Why Track B
+
+The paper is a complete classification, so this is not a Track A claim.  A direct
+implementation of the proof solves the generated distribution in `O(c log q)`:
+extract `d` and use one extended-Euclidean inverse per component.  At the shipping
+preset that compact route takes 230 arithmetic steps on the measured seed and 239
+on average across the eight attack seeds.  The disclosed mechanical reference
+algorithm instead scans all `q-1` classes from Theorem 3.12 for each component.  It
+uses exactly 6,000,120 congruence comparisons and averaged about 0.53 seconds here.
+The claimed difficulty is the no-tool gap between that six-million-test route and
+recognizing and accurately executing the compact invariant across 20 components.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+For `make_instance(n=5, components=1, redundant_generators=0, seed=0)`, the module
+uses `p=11`, `q=5`, `g=4` and displays the generators
+`[4,0,1,1]` and `[0,4,4,0]`.  Thus `d=4`, so the class is `mu=5` (the representative
+of residue zero in the paper's inclusive range `2..q`).
+
+```python
+demo = make_instance(n=5, components=1, redundant_generators=0, seed=0)
+verify(demo, [5])  # (True, "ok")
+verify(demo, [4])  # (False, "wrong A_mu class at component 0")
+```
+
+This smallest preset is genuinely hand-solvable: it requires checking four class
+labels, or recognizing one inverse modulo 5.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| Preset | q | Components | Generators/component | Class comparisons | Ships? |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 5 | 1 | 2 | 4 | no; worked example |
+| easy | 1,009 | 4 | 4 | 4,032 | no |
+| medium | 10,007 | 10 | 6 | 100,060 | no |
+| hard | 300,007 | 20 | 8 | 6,000,120 | intended shipping preset, pending G9 |
+
+## Gate results
+
+| Gate | Result | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted and compact-decoded witnesses verify; 12/12 JSON round trips |
+| G2 | pass | 6/6 corruptions rejected with six distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged JSON recovered from prose and a Markdown fence |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; 363-bit bounded language |
+| G5 | pass | shipping density sample 0/200,000; exactly one mathematical answer; reference 6,000,120 comparisons |
+| G6 | pass | four attacks each 0/8; reference scan 8/8 as expected |
+| G7 | pass | doubling `n` raises `q` 300,007 to 600,011 and space 363 to 383 bits; answer remains 20 atoms |
+| G8 | pass | 80/80 presentation relabellings invariant and carried witnesses valid; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | pass | 130 characters, 33 estimated tokens, 20 atoms, 230 arithmetic operations |
+| G9(b) | **blocked** | no scored oracle call; all three arms hit OpenRouter HTTP 403 total-limit errors |
+
+The four failing attacks are translation-magnitude rank, greedy copying of the
+visible second projection, 256 uniform distinct-list restarts, and the natural but
+off-by-one `d^-1` ansatz.  The successful exhaustive class scan is correctly
+reported under `reference_algorithm`, not among Track B failures.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+| Arm | Scored solved/attempts | Infrastructure calls | Result |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| bare | 0/0 | 4/4 HTTP 403 | no verdict |
+| structural hint | 0/0 | 4/4 HTTP 403 | no verdict |
+| placebo hint | 0/0 | 4/4 HTTP 403 | no verdict |
+
+The hinted-minus-placebo statistic is undefined in substance (stored as `0.0`
+because both denominators are zero).  Nothing can yet be concluded about whether
+the invariant hint helps.  The transcripts are preserved as infrastructure
+evidence, not hardness evidence.  After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun the bare
+harness in this directory and each G9 arm in its own scratch directory, update
+`G9_ORACLE_RESULTS`, regenerate `selftest_report.json`, and only ship if G9 passes.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_1908_03228 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, render, parse_answer, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+prompt = render(inst)
+candidate = parse_answer("<answer>[...]</answer>")
+ok, reason = verify(inst, candidate)
+```
+
+From the repository root, emit instances with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1908.03228 20
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+This family becomes easy with a CAS, GAP/Magma, or the displayed Theorem 3.12
+formula; that is precisely why it is Track B.  The guess probability is measured
+under the stated uniform distribution on ordered, pairwise-distinct class lists;
+it does not model a solver prior informed by group theory.  Planted bundles are
+additionally conditioned to need at most 280 Euclidean steps, so their distribution
+is not identical to that candidate prior (valid-answer density is still exactly one
+candidate per instance).  No computer-algebra
+package or additional group-isomorphism algorithm was tested.  The canonical key
+is complete for this generator's conjugation, generator-order, redundancy, and
+component-order symmetries, not for arbitrary skew braces.  Most importantly, the
+four-vendor oracle and hinted G9 checks remain unmeasured until the external quota
+block is removed; local correctness evidence must not be mistaken for a hardness
+verdict.
