454:% 	Let $A$ be a group. There exists a bijective correspondence between skew brace structures with additive group isomorphic to $A$ and regular subgroups of $\Hol(A)$. Moreover, isomorphic skew brace structures correspond to conjugate subgroups of $\Hol(A)$ by elements of $\Aut{A}$.
462:% 	The set of Hopf--Galois structures of type $A$ on a Galois extension of fields with group $G$ corresponds bijectively to the set of orbits $\mathcal{G}/\Aut(G)$, while the set of isomorphism classes of skew braces with multiplicative group $G$ and additive group $A$ corresponds bijectively to the set of orbits $\mathcal{G}/(\Aut(G)\times \Aut(A))$.
467:% In other words, given an explicit description of the regular subgroups of $\Hol(A)$ for a group $A$ one can construct all the skew braces with additive group isomorphic to $A$ by finding representatives of the orbits under the action by conjugation of $\Aut(A)$ in $\Hol(A)$. To this end, we use results from Byott \cite{Byott_pq} in which all Hopf--Galois extensions of order $pq$ for $p,q$ different primes have been classified. 
