codex
The solve was not a malformed-parser issue—the oracle returned exact class vectors. I found the weakness: the current hard preset asks for 20 unrelated inversions, and modern models can execute that directly. I’m strengthening the same theorem-backed family without lengthening the witness past the cap: 128 class labels are planted as one affine progression, so the compact route needs only two inversions plus recurrence, while the structure-aware mechanical scan still takes over \(2\times10^7\) exact tests at shipping size. This changes the task from repeated calculator work into recognizing and exploiting a global invariant.
apply patch
