The strengthened family passed G1–G7 and G9(c), but G8 exposed a real modeling bug: the new progression is indexed, while the old relabeling test renumbered components arbitrarily and thereby destroyed that structure. I’m fixing the representation so component-list order is presentation-only and stable component indices carry the progression; arbitrary input reordering will then preserve both the problem and the original witness.
