codex
The indexed progression fix works, but it also revealed a better hardening axis. A consecutive recurrence is still easy for a model once two labels are known. I’m replacing the index \(r\) by a displayed, randomly scattered field coordinate \(t_r\), with class residues on one hidden affine function \(u+v t_r\). The certificate remains 112 integers; the compact route stays below 300 exact operations, while the remaining labels now require genuine modular multiplications rather than transcription of a simple sequence.
